* LM741 Op-Amp - Behavioral Macromodel
* Compatible with Veronese 7-pin symbol: in+ in- V+ V- out comp1 comp2
* Open-loop gain: 200,000 V/V | Output clamps near supply rails
*
.subckt LM741v 1 2 3 4 5 6 7
* Pin 1=in+  2=in-  3=V+  4=V-  5=out  6=comp1  7=comp2
*
* Compensation pins (unused - avoid floating nodes)
Rdum1 6 0 1G
Rdum2 7 0 1G
*
* Input impedance (2 Megohm, typical LM741)
Rin 1 2 2Meg
*
* High-gain stage with output clamping to rails
* Output saturates at Vee+1.5 to Vcc-1.5 (typical for LM741)
B1 mid 0 V = limit(200000*V(1,2), V(4)+1.5, V(3)-1.5)
*
* Output resistance (75 ohm typical)
Rout mid 5 75
*
* Slew rate approximation (C on output node: ~0.5 V/us)
Csr 5 0 100n
*
* Quiescent supply current
ISS 3 4 1.7m
*
.ends LM741v
